# A method's typed reference `@: Model r` (its local, D-76) is rebound only after the admission of the value to Model --
# implements(mo, Model, Model), the interim structural admission the walked root's calls too, for a Model's own as well,
# no shortcut (OPUS-CALLABLE-STRUCT-BINDING-20260929-16, step 2).  mo's 7 read through r, and a write through r is mo's.
# Entry 7.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

fn: check () int
    Model: mo
    @: Model r
    size_t: v 0U
    int: out 0
    mo\value: 7U
    r: @mo
    v: r\value
    if: v = 7U
        out: 3
    r\value: 9U
    v: mo\value
    if: v = 9U
        out: out + 4
    return: out
end: check

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
